A1. These are inveterate smokers. ~ STACKS
A6. What was the Charge of the Light Brigade? ~ ATTACK
A11. Crosswordists have this angle down to a T. ~ ELL
A12. To start the disappearing act. ~ EBB
A13. It's unhealthy to be this way. ~ ILL
A15. You should keep this with the times. ~ ABREAST
A18. A famous Frenchman who figured out everything under the sun. ~ LAPLACE
A21. This starts percolating and ends supper. ~ PER
A22. This should be kept for the old folks. ~ RESPECT
A24. A wide-awake burglar wouldn't take this. ~ NAP
A25. A wise guy often bites on this kind of money. ~ LEADEN
A27. This sticks through thick and thin. ~ COCKLE
A29. This is ruinous. ~ CATASTROPHE
A32. What trysters should never be. ~ SEEN
A34. A clannish thing about the American Indian. ~ TOTEM
A35. Anyone who puts two and two together does this. ~ ADDS
A37. A silly, sappy person. (Modern slang.) ~ GOOF
A38. The wit of Henry the Eighth. ~ FOOL
A39. This gets a lot of devotion. ~ IDOL
A41. Stormed. ~ RAGED
A43. Where some people go when they are out. (Plural.) ~ INNS
A46. What a widower needs to marry again. ~ REASSURANCE
A49. A condition found in large dry areas. ~ DEARTH
A51. Something elevating about golf. (Two words) (Plural.) ~ TEEUPS
A53. A crossword eagle. ~ ERN
A54. What any married man becomes when he returns home at 3 A. M. ~ TIPTOER
A57. What old ladies do to get a trimming. ~ TAT
A58. When this gets the air it makes an awful racket. ~ BAGPIPE
A60. Bad circumstances to get caught in. ~ ADVERSE
A62. An organ. ~ EAR
A63. An animal with prominent teeth. ~ ELK
A64. A little lady famous before the Civil War. ~ EVA
A65. What day-dreamers are. ~ ASLEEP
A66. What tourists hear about Switzerland. (Plural.) ~ YODELS

D2. This takes a drop at a time. ~ TERRACE
D3. A crossword beverage. ~ ALE
D4. A kind of wine. ~ CLARET
D5. What bedroom furniture comes in. ~ SETS
D6. This kind of person is competent. ~ ABLE
D7. How a person feels who is sitting on top of the world. ~ TIPTOP
D8. Half and half. ~ ALL
D9. How knights of yore came downstairs. ~ CLANKED
D10. Green shades. ~ MAPLES
D14. What ugliness does. ~ REPELS
D16. A non-electric buzzer. ~ BEE
D17. Another kind of air-craft. ~ SENATORSHIP
D19. What an heiress gets when she wants a date. ~ ACCOMODATED
D20. A well-known personage who will soon lose his job. ~ CAL
D23. The golfer is successful when this sinks in. ~ PUTT
D26. A man at the end of his rope. ~ DANGLER
D28. The cup that Galahad competed for. ~ CHALICE
D30. Where young men get set on. (Plural.) ~ SOFAS
D31. To trace or ascribe to person or thing. ~ REFER
D33. This is the finish. ~ END
D36. This gets noised about. ~ DIN
D39. How wives keep their husbands. (Two words.) ~ INDEBT
D40. Seedy Floridans. ~ ORANGES
D42. This is breezy. ~ GUST
D44. This kind of person never takes sides. ~ NEUTRAL
D45. The girl who gets left behind. ~ SISTER
D47. There's not much of this to the modern girl. ~ ATTIRE
D48. Stiffened the vertebrae. ~ NERVED
D50. A period. ~ ERA
D52. French step ~ PAS
D55. Our way of looking at it. ~ PEEP
D56. Like an oak. ~ OAKY
D59. This is companionate. ~ PAL
D61. When the outlook is kind of dark. ~ EVE


